# sg-content

## Mission

`sg-content` is the public owner for editorial brand expression, public documentation, and audience content.

## Scope Gate

Resolve the product, audience, and public surface, then load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`. Own the public-content outcome from source and claims through validation and publication readiness.

## Required References

Resolve `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT` through the shared canonical-path doctrine, verify the root and `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/007-sg-content/SKILL.md` exist, then load that canonical engine for the detailed content lifecycle. If the root or file is missing, stop with a visible error; never fall back to a sibling runtime path. Keep internal editorial engines invisible to the operator; `007-sg-content` is expert/legacy only.

## Validation

Use the selected lifecycle's source, claim, audience-fit, and publication-readiness proof.

## Stop Conditions

Stop and follow the runtime contract when the audience, claims, publication authority, or required proof is unresolved.

## Report Modes

Load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before reporting; keep internal engine names out of user-facing reports.
